# Adapter outputs under .testatlas/adapters/<name>/<dotdir>/ ARE tracked —
# they're the suite's per-adapter rendered content that installers copy
# into target repos. Without these negations, the bare `.claude/` /
# `.cursor/` / etc. patterns above match the nested adapter paths and
# silently drop new files at `git add` time (e.g. atlas-create-persona.md
# was missing from origin until 2026-05-10, breaking every adapter-parity
# test in CI; the file was on disk locally but `git add` was a no-op).
# The grandfather rule means already-tracked files keep being tracked,
# but newly-generated adapter files for new source commands were
# invisibly dropped. The negations below restore visibility for the
# whole `.testatlas/adapters/` subtree.
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.claude/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.cursor/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.opencode/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.kilocode/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.aider/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.windsurf/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.continue/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.cline/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.codex/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.gemini/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.roo/
!.testatlas/adapters/**/.kiro/
